\pgfsyspdfmark {pgfid1}{5644739}{50063931}
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {section}{\numberline {1}The gap a reader found}{1}{section.1}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces \small  The two provenance gaps, closed by the same key. A released binary carries a require-both seal (verifiable, \textcolor {sigilcyan}{$\text  {$\mathsurround \z@ \mathchar "458$}$}); the promise around it carries none (silently editable, $\times $). The same signer (\texttt  {flux-rev} / require-both) that attests the artifact attests the words --- one key, two things worth proving.}}{2}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {section}{\numberline {2}Why a provenance chain owes this to itself}{2}{section.2}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {section}{\numberline {3}The primitives already exist (because we built the stack)}{2}{section.3}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces \small  One vertical spine, all of it ours: Flux compiler \,$\to $\, content-addressing \,$\to $\, require-both signing \,$\to $\, the braid / event-log root \,$\to $\, the fold \,$\to $\, at the cap, a Commitment Record witnessed \emph  {inside} (seal) and \emph  {outside} (a Bitcoin receipt). Solid layers are live; dashed layers are staged --- the honesty is drawn into the diagram.}}{3}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {section}{\numberline {4}The Commitment Record}{3}{section.4}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {section}{\numberline {5}Verification, a year later}{4}{section.5}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {section}{\numberline {6}Independent time: borrowing Bitcoin's clock}{4}{section.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{sec:time}{{6}{4}{Independent time: borrowing Bitcoin's clock}{section.6}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces \small  You cannot be your own witness. The promise key, the record chain, and the anchoring chain are one hand (the closed \textcolor {sigilviolet}{violet} loop); a Commitment Record breaks the circle by also stamping onto \textcolor {sigilamber}{Bitcoin} --- an authority we do not control. SIGIL proves \emph  {inclusion}; Bitcoin proves the \emph  {time}.}}{5}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {section}{\numberline {7}What this does not do (scope, stated plainly)}{5}{section.7}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {section}{\numberline {8}The recursion, and this note as its seed}{6}{section.8}\protected@file@percent }
\gdef \@abspage@last{6}
